# descope_project (Resource)

Manages a Descope project. A project is the core entity in Descope—its authentication settings, user flows, roles, connectors, applications, and other configuration are managed with the standalone `descope_*` resources that reference the project by ID.

This resource manages _project configuration_, not users or tenants. For user management, use the [Descope Management API](https://docs.descope.com/api/openapi) or [SDKs](https://docs.descope.com).

For a full reference of all supported connectors, see the [connectors reference](https://docs.descope.com/connectors) in the Descope documentation.

## Example Usage

### Basic Project

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name        = "my-app"
  environment = "production"
  tags        = ["prod", "v2"]
}
```

### Authentication Methods

Authentication method settings are managed with their own standalone resources, such as
[`descope_magiclink_settings`](./magiclink_settings), [`descope_otp_settings`](./otp_settings),
[`descope_password_settings`](./password_settings), and [`descope_sso_settings`](./sso_settings):

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_magiclink_settings" "example" {
  project_id      = descope_project.example.id
  expiration_time = "1 hour"
}

resource "descope_password_settings" "example" {
  project_id    = descope_project.example.id
  lock          = true
  lock_attempts = 5
  min_length    = 12
}
```

### Roles and Permissions (RBAC)

Roles and permissions are managed as standalone resources that reference the project by ID:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_permission" "read_data" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "read:data"
  description = "Read access to application data"
}

resource "descope_permission" "write_data" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "write:data"
  description = "Write access to application data"
}

resource "descope_permission" "admin_panel" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "admin:panel"
  description = "Access to the admin panel"
}

resource "descope_role" "viewer" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "viewer"
  description = "Can read data"
  permissions = [descope_permission.read_data.name]
}

resource "descope_role" "editor" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "editor"
  description = "Can read and write data"
  permissions = [descope_permission.read_data.name, descope_permission.write_data.name]
}

resource "descope_role" "admin" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "admin"
  description = "Full access"
  permissions = [descope_permission.read_data.name, descope_permission.write_data.name, descope_permission.admin_panel.name]
}
```

### Connectors

Integrate with third-party services using standalone per-type connector resources:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

# Generic HTTP webhook with bearer token auth
resource "descope_http_connector" "eligibility" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "User Eligibility Check"
  description = "Checks if a new user is allowed to register"
  base_url    = "https://api.example.com"
  authentication = {
    bearer_token = var.webhook_secret
  }
}

# SendGrid for email delivery
resource "descope_sendgrid_connector" "email" {
  project_id   = descope_project.example.id
  name         = "Transactional Email"
  sender_email = "noreply@example.com"
  sender_name  = "My App"
  api_key      = var.sendgrid_api_key
}

# Twilio for SMS OTP
resource "descope_twilio_core_connector" "sms" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "SMS OTP"
  account_sid = var.twilio_account_sid
  from_phone  = "+15551234567"
  auth_token  = var.twilio_auth_token
}
```

### Flows and Styles

Load custom authentication flows and styles from JSON files (exported from the Descope
console) with the standalone `descope_flow` and `descope_styles` resources:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_flow" "sign_up_or_in" {
  project_id = descope_project.example.id
  flow_id    = "sign-up-or-in"
  data       = file("${path.module}/flows/sign-up-or-in.json")
}

resource "descope_styles" "example" {
  project_id = descope_project.example.id
  data       = file("${path.module}/flows/styles.json")
}
```

### Project and Session Settings

General project settings, session behavior, and user invitations are managed with the
standalone [`descope_project_settings`](./project_settings),
[`descope_session_settings`](./session_settings), and
[`descope_invite_settings`](./invite_settings) resources:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_project_settings" "example" {
  project_id       = descope_project.example.id
  app_url          = "https://app.example.com"
  approved_domains = ["example.com", "app.example.com"]
}

resource "descope_session_settings" "example" {
  project_id               = descope_project.example.id
  refresh_token_expiration = "3 weeks"
  session_token_expiration = "15 minutes"
  refresh_token_rotation   = true
  enable_inactivity        = true
  inactivity_time          = "30 minutes"
}

resource "descope_invite_settings" "example" {
  project_id         = descope_project.example.id
  require_invitation = true
  invite_url         = "https://app.example.com/invite"
}
```

### Federated Applications

Federated (SSO IdP) applications and their app-scoped roles and permissions are managed
with the standalone `descope_oidc_app`, `descope_saml_app`, `descope_wsfed_app`,
`descope_app_role`, and `descope_app_permission` resources that reference the project by ID:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_oidc_app" "web" {
  project_id     = descope_project.example.id
  name           = "My Web App"
  description    = "Primary web application"
  login_page_url = "https://app.example.com/login"
}

resource "descope_app_permission" "read_reports" {
  project_id = descope_project.example.id
  app_id     = descope_oidc_app.web.id
  name       = "read:reports"
}

resource "descope_app_role" "analyst" {
  project_id     = descope_project.example.id
  app_id         = descope_oidc_app.web.id
  name           = "analyst"
  permission_ids = [descope_app_permission.read_reports.id]
}
```

### JWT Templates

JWT templates are managed with the standalone `descope_jwt_template` resource that
references the project by ID:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_jwt_template" "app_claims" {
  project_id  = descope_project.example.id
  name        = "app-claims"
  description = "Adds subscription tier and org context to user JWTs"
  type        = "user"
  template    = jsonencode({
    tier   = "@user.customAttributes.subscriptionTier"
    org_id = "@user.tenants[0].tenantId"
  })

  # Exclude the permissions claim to keep tokens lean
  exclude_permission_claim = true

  # Add a unique JWT ID for replay attack prevention
  add_jti_claim = true

  # Move the user ID to a new dsub claim, allowing sub to be customized
  override_subject_claim = true
}
```

### SSO Settings

Global settings for Single Sign-On across tenants are managed with the standalone
[`descope_sso_settings`](./sso_settings) resource:

```hcl
resource "descope_project" "example" {
  name = "my-app"
}

resource "descope_sso_settings" "example" {
  project_id = descope_project.example.id

  # Merge SSO users with existing accounts of the same email
  merge_users = true

  # Allow SSO roles to override a user's existing roles
  allow_override_roles = true

  # Define required Descope attributes when receiving SSO information
  mandatory_user_attributes = [
    { id = "email" },
    { id = "name" },
    { id = "department", custom = true },
  ]

  # Configure the SSO Suite portal appearance
  sso_suite_settings = {
    style_id  = "my-brand-style"
    hide_scim = false
    hide_saml = false
    hide_oidc = false
  }
}
```


